<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ghiyath al-Din Muhammad</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1139–1203</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Ghiyath al-Din Muhammad of Ghor</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ghiyath al-Din Muhammad was sultan of the Ghurid dynasty from 1163 to 1203, ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/firozkoh">Firozkoh</a> in the mountains of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghor">Ghor</a> and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herat">Herat</a>. He shared power with his brother Mu'izz al-Din Muhammad, who led the conquests in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, while he himself fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khwarazmians">Khwarazmians</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khorasan">Khorasan</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/minaret-of-jam">Minaret of Jam</a> is attributed to his reign.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ghiyath-al-din-muhammad.jpg" alt="Ghiyath al-Din Muhammad" width="320" height="309" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ninara · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ghiyath_al-Din_Muhammad.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
